From 61c827f26d9a6b8a070e9022f9807dbe01a2fd65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:31:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Time capsule: skyline extents shrink back to the towers built
 by the chosen year

With the time capsule on, the skyline extent layer shows public/skyline-extent-years.geojson instead of
today's drawn cores: each core trimmed to the area within 400 m of the towers completed by that year,
plus the gaps between them once the towers around a gap have been built, closed by 300 m and clipped to
the core, so an extent only grows with time and never reaches past today's line. A city's extent
appears once 5 towers in its core stand; from the year of its core's latest tower on it is the drawn
core itself. Clicking an extent says how many of the core's towers stood that year and the tallest.

The file is made at build time by scripts/skyline-years.mjs (run from prebuild, using jsts for the
geometry), from public/skyline-extent.geojson and towers.json, so a revised cores file or new tower
data is picked up on the next build; it is skipped when neither has changed since the last run.

